{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_011CfSZXFMUaHUGajocQp6rh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:DESIGN>>\n```\n\n**Proposed change, file by file:**\n\n1. **Order.kt** - Add `status: OrderStatus` field to Order data class, defaulting to ACTIVE. Create OrderStatus enum with ACTIVE and CANCELLED values.\n\n2. **OrderRepository.kt** - Add method `findByOrderId` to find shipments (wait, no, I need to add it to ShipmentRepository). Actually, no changes needed here.\n\n3. **ShipmentRepository.kt** - Add `findByOrderId(orderId: String): List<Shipment>` method to retrieve all shipments for an order.\n\n4. **OrderController.kt** - Add `@PostMapping(\"/{orderId}/cancel\")` endpoint that:\n   - Finds the order by ID (throw ResourceNotFoundException if not found)\n   - If order is already CANCELLED, return the order and change nothing (idempotent)\n   - Check if any shipment of the order is CONFIRMED; if so, throw ConflictException and change nothing (all-or-nothing)\n   - Otherwise, move order to CANCELLED status\n   - Cancel all CREATED shipments by setting their status to CANCELLED\n   - Persist changes and return the cancelled order\n\n5. **ShipmentController.kt** - In the create endpoint, before saving a new shipment:\n   - Fetch the order (optional: only if needed)\n   - Check if order status is CANCELLED; if so, throw ConflictException\n\n6. **ApiError.kt** - Add two new ErrorCode values:\n   - `ORDER_CANNOT_BE_CANCELLED` (for when trying to cancel an order with CONFIRMED shipments)\n   - `ORDER_IS_CANCELLED` (for when trying to create a shipment for a cancelled order)\n\n7. **OrderControllerTest.kt** - Add tests:\n   - Cancel an active order succeeds and moves shipments to CANCELLED\n   - Cancel an already cancelled order succeeds and changes nothing (idempotent)\n   - Cancel an order with CONFIRMED shipment returns 409 and changes nothing\n   - Cancel non-existent order returns 404\n   - Verify GET /orders/{orderId} returns correct status\n\n8. **ShipmentControllerTest.kt** - Add tests:\n   - Creating a shipment for a CANCELLED order returns 409\n\n**Alternatives rejected:**\n\n1. **Using OrderService layer** - Could add an OrderService class to encapsulate the cancellation logic. However, the existing code patterns show controllers directly calling repositories, so adding a service would introduce unnecessary complexity and break existing conventions.\n\n2. **Propagating status through shipment responses** - Could return the order's status in shipment responses. But the requirement doesn't ask for this, and it would add unnecessary coupling. Rejected.\n\n3. **Using a separate Cancel order status** - Could have ACTIVE, CANCELLED_PENDING, CANCELLED. The requirement only mentions ACTIVE and CANCELLED, so keeping it simple. Rejected.\n\n**Data and error flow:**\n\n*Happy path - Cancel active order with CREATED shipments:*\n1. POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel → OrderController.cancel()\n2. OrderRepository.findById(orderId) → returns Order with status=ACTIVE\n3. ShipmentRepository.findByOrderId(orderId) → returns list of Shipments\n4. Check: no CONFIRMED shipments\n5. Create new Order with status=CANCELLED, save via OrderRepository.save()\n6. For each CREATED shipment: create new Shipment with status=CANCELLED, save\n7. Return updated Order (200 OK)\n\n*Idempotent cancel - Already CANCELLED order:*\n1. POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel → OrderController.cancel()\n2. OrderRepository.findById(orderId) → returns Order with status=CANCELLED\n3. Check: status is CANCELLED, return immediately with the same order (200 OK)\n4. Nothing changes\n\n*Error case - CONFIRMED shipment exists:*\n1. POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel → OrderController.cancel()\n2. OrderRepository.findById(orderId) → returns Order with status=ACTIVE\n3. ShipmentRepository.findByOrderId(orderId) → returns list including CONFIRMED shipment\n4. Check: CONFIRMED shipment found → throw ConflictException(ORDER_CANNOT_BE_CANCELLED, ...)\n5. GlobalExceptionHandler catches and returns 409 with error envelope\n6. Order stays ACTIVE, shipments unchanged\n\n*Error case - Non-existent order:*\n1. POST /orders/{orderId}/cancel → OrderController.cancel()\n2. OrderRepository.findById(orderId) → returns null\n3. Throw ResourceNotFoundException(ORDER_NOT_FOUND, ...)\n4. GlobalExceptionHandler catches and returns 404 with error envelope\n\n*Shipment creation with CANCELLED order:*\n1. POST /shipments → ShipmentController.create()\n2. Check for duplicate shipment ID (existing logic)\n3. **NEW**: OrderRepository.findById(orderId) → returns Order with status=CANCELLED\n4. **NEW**: Throw ConflictException(ORDER_IS_CANCELLED, ...)\n5. GlobalExceptionHandler catches and returns 409 with error envelope\n\n**Test strategy:**\n\n1. **OrderControllerTest.cancel_active_order_succeeds()** - Create order, create CREATED shipment, cancel order, verify order status=CANCELLED and shipment status=CANCELLED\n2. **OrderControllerTest.cancel_already_cancelled_order_succeeds()** - Create order, cancel it, cancel again, verify 200 OK and no changes\n3. **OrderControllerTest.cancel_with_confirmed_shipment_returns_409()** - Create order, create CONFIRMED shipment, cancel order, verify 409 with ORDER_CANNOT_BE_CANCELLED error code, verify order still ACTIVE\n4. **OrderControllerTest.cancel_non_existent_order_returns_404()** - Cancel non-existent order, verify 404 with ORDER_NOT_FOUND error code\n5. **OrderControllerTest.get_order_returns_status()** - Create order, verify status=ACTIVE in GET response; cancel order, verify status=CANCELLED in GET response\n6. **ShipmentControllerTest.create_for_cancelled_order_returns_409()** - Create order, cancel it, try to create shipment, verify 409 with ORDER_IS_CANCELLED error code\n\n---\n\n```\n<<PHASE:IMPLEMENTATION>>\n```\n\nNow I'll implement the changes according to the design. Let me start:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":8,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1200,"cache_read_input_tokens":23957,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1200},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5b0aad69-6ae2-4332-9daf-ace377f18b7a","uuid":"6ebe014b-3dcf-4bd5-93fe-90406324184a","timestamp":"2026-09-26T18:56:59.156Z","request_id":"req_011CfSZXEyB1WhjJ1hSDdgdj"}
